{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"913cdb06348a3b71b7009dac7b313a3661b4aac3ec9a934b3164944a442b44d8","digest":{"component_or_area":"test suite / wiki render hardening","key_entities":["tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py","test_rendered_output_is_byte_identical_to_the_landed_renderer","_renderable_units","_EQUIVALENCE_CHUNK","_EQUIVALENCE_STRIDE","_convert","_legacy_convert","pytest-timeout","--timeout=300","--timeout-method=thread",".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","test_the_equivalence_chunks_cover_every_renderable_unit"],"problem_keywords":["flaky ci","test timeout","pytest-xdist worker crash","macos","unbounded test cost","pandoc"],"propositions":["The test kills its pytest-xdist worker intermittently on macOS py3.13 when pytest-timeout's thread method calls os._exit(1) after the 300s per-test budget is exceeded.","The test's unbounded serial cost walks 884 renderable units with ~1768 pandoc spawns in a single test function, measuring 91.6s idle and 504.8s under CPU saturation—1.7x past the 300s guard.","Chunking the test with fixed-size batches (_EQUIVALENCE_CHUNK=40) bounds per-test cost by construction so corpus growth adds cases rather than extending any case, preventing future timeout re-crossing.","All 884 units remain compared against the oracle with real pandoc at stride 1, preserving the byte-identity property the test protects, while xdist spreads work across workers instead of pinning to one."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787300650505606001,"uuid":"e91cc651-951e-429c-b567-cc4a006299f7"}